D('hint',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'She gave us a hint that the final exam would include a map question.','她暗示期末考试会有一道地图题。'),ex(2,'The guide offered a hint about where the missing key might be.','向导给了一条关于失踪钥匙可能位置的提示。'),ex(3,'There was a hint of smoke in the air after the wiring overheated.','电线过热后，空气中有一丝烟味。'),ex(4,'The manager hinted at a schedule change without giving a date.','经理暗示日程会有变动，却没有给出日期。')],mistakes:[m('grammar','He hinted me that the meeting had moved.','He hinted to me that the meeting had moved.','hint 作动词通常说 hint to someone that…，不能直接以人作间接宾语。')],quiz:[q('hint',1,1,'A hint about a surprise party is _____.','an indirect suggestion','a full written contract','a loud announcement of every detail','hint 可指间接给出的暗示。'),q('hint',2,2,'A puzzle hint offers a player _____.','a small clue','the complete score report','a new game console','名词 hint 也指帮助解题的线索或提示。'),q('hint',3,3,'“A hint of lemon” means _____.','a very small amount of lemon','a whole lemon tree','no lemon flavor whatsoever','a hint of 可表示一丝或少量。'),q('hint',4,4,'Which sentence uses hint as a verb correctly?','She hinted at a possible delay.','She hinted the passengers at a delay.','She hinted to delay at the passengers.','hint at something 是自然的动词搭配。')]});
