D('hip',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'The cyclist fell onto her hip but stood up without help.','骑行者摔到了髋部，但自己站了起来。'),ex(2,'The trousers fit at the waist but felt tight around the hips.','这条裤子腰围合适，但臀围处感觉很紧。'),ex(3,'The jam was made from wild rose hips picked in autumn.','这款果酱是用秋天采摘的野蔷薇果制成的。'),ex(4,'The once-empty warehouse is now a hip place for live music.','这座曾经空置的仓库如今成了听现场音乐的时髦场所。')],mistakes:[m('word form','The hips joint was sore after the fall.','The hip joint was sore after the fall.','复合名词 hip joint 用 hip 作定语，不用复数 hips。')],quiz:[q('hip',1,1,'A doctor examines a patient’s hip after a fall. Which area is meant?','the joint at the side of the pelvis','the wrist','the shoulder blade','hip 指腿上方身体两侧的髋部。'),q('hip',2,2,'If a skirt is tight at the hips, it is tight around the _____.','part covering the wearer’s hips','ankles','collar','hip 可指衣物覆盖臀部的部分。'),q('hip',3,3,'Rose hips are _____.','the fruit of a wild rose','a type of bird','a hip-shaped garden tool','rose hip 指野蔷薇的果实。'),q('hip',4,4,'A hip café is described as _____.','fashionable and trendy','located only on a hillside','medically unsafe','口语形容词 hip 表示时髦的。')]});
D('hip-hop',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'The dance class uses hip-hop tracks with a strong, syncopated beat.','舞蹈课使用节拍鲜明、带切分节奏的嘻哈乐曲。')],mistakes:[m('spelling','The DJ played hiphop throughout the competition.','The DJ played hip-hop throughout the competition.','标准拼写带连字符：hip-hop。')],quiz:[q('hip-hop',1,1,'A hip-hop track is most closely associated with _____.','rhythmic popular music and rap culture','a classical string quartet','a silent film score','hip-hop 指源自街头文化的音乐类型。'),q('hip-hop',2,1,'Which is the standard written form?','hip-hop','hiphop','hip hop-hop','词条标准拼写为 hip-hop。'),q('hip-hop',3,1,'A hip-hop dance class would most likely practice to _____.','a beat-driven track','a spoken weather report','a violin tuning exercise only','嘻哈舞蹈常伴随节奏鲜明的音乐。'),q('hip-hop',4,1,'In “She listens to hip-hop,” the word is a _____.','music genre','musical instrument','dance venue','此处 hip-hop 作不可数音乐类型名词。')]});
D('hire',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'The studio hired a lighting designer for the six-week production.','工作室为期六周的制作聘请了一位灯光设计师。'),ex(2,'They hired a small van to move the display panels.','他们租了一辆小货车搬运展板。'),ex(3,'The bicycles are available for hire beside the station.','车站旁的自行车可供租用。'),ex(4,'The hire of the town hall includes use of its kitchen.','租用市政厅还包括使用厨房。')],mistakes:[m('grammar','We hired a kayak on two hours.','We hired a kayak for two hours.','表示租用时长用 for two hours，不用 on two hours。')],quiz:[q('hire',1,1,'A company hires an engineer. It _____.','employs the engineer','borrows the engineer’s car','pays the engineer to rent an office','hire 作动词可表示聘用某人。'),q('hire',2,2,'They hired a boat for the afternoon. They _____.','paid to use it temporarily','bought it permanently','gave it away','hire 也可表示付费短期租用物品。'),q('hire',3,3,'“The bikes are for hire” means the bikes are _____.','available to rent','being given away','out of service permanently','名词 hire 可指租赁服务或可供出租。'),q('hire',4,4,'“The hire of the hall cost £200” refers to _____.','the act or arrangement of renting the hall','the wages of the hall manager','the purchase of the hall','hire 作名词也可指租用行为。')]});
