D('his',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'Noah left his notebook beside the microscope.','诺亚把他的笔记本落在显微镜旁。'),ex(2,'My umbrella is blue, but his is green.','我的伞是蓝色的，而他的伞是绿色的。')],mistakes:[m('grammar','The notebook is him.','The notebook is his.','表示“这本笔记本是他的”用名词性物主代词 his，him 是宾格。')],quiz:[q('his',1,1,'Complete: “Eli forgot ___ coat on the train.”','his','him','he','名词前作限定词用 his。'),q('his',2,2,'“That seat is his” means it belongs to _____.','him','he','himself only','句末独立使用时 his 是名词性物主代词。'),q('his',3,1,'Which sentence uses his as a determiner?','His keys are on the desk.','The keys are his.','The keys were handed to him.','his 后接名词 keys，因此作限定词。'),q('his',4,2,'Choose the correct completion: “My ticket is here; ___ is in her bag.”','his','him','he','名词性物主代词 his 可独立代指 his ticket。')]});
D('historic',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'The two rival communities signed a historic agreement after decades of negotiation.','经过数十年谈判，两个对立社群签署了一项具有历史意义的协议。')],mistakes:[m('word choice','The museum gives a historic account of daily life in the 1800s.','The museum gives a historical account of daily life in the 1800s.','这里指“关于历史的记述”，用 historical；historic 通常强调事件具有重大历史意义。')],quiz:[q('historic',1,1,'A historic agreement is one that is _____.','important enough to be remembered in history','merely old with no special importance','about weather in the present','historic 强调事件本身具有历史意义。'),q('historic',2,1,'Which event is most naturally called historic?','the first peaceful election after a long conflict','an ordinary lunch break','a routine weekly staff meeting','改变历史进程的首次和平选举可称 historic。'),q('historic',3,1,'Choose the best word: “The archive contains ___ documents from the war.”','historical','historic','historically','说明文件与历史时期有关时用 historical。'),q('historic',4,1,'A historic first flight is one that _____.','marks an important milestone','is simply scheduled for yesterday','has no record or significance','historic 带有重要里程碑的含义。')]});
